CloudBurrow patch 19 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1189). Needs go-googlesql patch 0002.

The bug: the analyzer folds a CAST of a literal, and coerces a literal to
a column's type, in its default zone, America/Los_Angeles; BigQuery's is
UTC. Measured on the emulator with patches 0001 to 0018:
CAST(DATE '2020-01-01' AS TIMESTAMP) and
CAST(DATETIME '2020-01-01 00:00:00' AS TIMESTAMP) were
2020-01-01 08:00 UTC; CAST(TIMESTAMP '2020-01-01 05:00:00+00' AS STRING)
was "2019-12-31 21:00:00-08"; a CAST of a TIMESTAMP literal to DATE,
DATETIME or TIME gave the Los Angeles date and time; and
TIMESTAMP '2020-01-01 05:00:00+00' = '2020-01-01 05:00:00' was false. Functions (TIMESTAMP(), DATE(ts), EXTRACT, FORMAT_TIMESTAMP and
the rest) run in Go, where no zone is UTC, and were already right.

The patch:
- sets the analyzer's default zone to UTC
  (SetDefaultTimeZone(googlesql.UTCTimeZone()));
- writes a TIMESTAMP cast to STRING at run time, a column's, as BigQuery
  does, "2020-01-01 05:00:00.500+00", where it was RFC 3339,
  "2020-01-01T05:00:00.5Z";
- STRING(ts, zone) wrote the text "+00" whatever the zone; it now writes
  the zone's offset, "2020-01-01 00:00:00-05", "+05:30";
- a STRING with a named zone, "2020-01-01 00:00:00 America/New_York",
  cast to TIMESTAMP at run time was refused; it is now read in that zone.
Patch 0018's rewrite of TIMESTAMP literals with no zone is kept: with the
default zone UTC it changes nothing.

